{{Quote|Soon the ''Eye of Sion'' will be complete and we shall deliver Grand Admiral Thrawn from his exile in the far galaxy.|Morgan Elsbeth|<ref name="P2" />}}
The '''far galaxy''' was a barred spiral [[galaxy]] that was one of trillions of [[Galaxy|galaxies]] in the [[Universe|observable universe]] and was [[extragalactic|distant]] from the [[The galaxy|galaxy]] of the [[New Republic]]. It contained the [[planet]] [[Peridea]], home to the great [[Witch Kingdom of the Dathmiri]], an ancient civilization, and the location of [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn's]] [[Exile (punishment)|exile]]. However, by then the galaxy was largely dead and barren, being wiped out by a [[Far galaxy war|war]].

The other galaxy's planet [[Seatos]] had a [[Seatos reflex point|henge]] that marked the [[Pathway to Peridea]]. [[Morgan Elsbeth]], a follower of Thrawn and a [[Dathomirian|Dathomiri]] [[Nightsisters|Nightsister]], built the interstellar [[hyperspace transport ring]] named the ''[[Eye of Sion]]'' to retrieve Thrawn and his stranded [[Thrawn's forces|forces]].

==History==
===Ancient times===
{{Quote|I see what once was the great Witch Kingdom of the Dathmiri. The existence of the Great Mothers confirms this.|Baylan Skoll|<ref name="P6" />}}
[[File:Peridea-Ahsoka-PartSix.png|left|thumb|240x240px|Peridea was once the heart of the Witch Kingdom of the Dathmiri.]]
The far galaxy<ref name="Databank">{{Databank|far-galaxy|Far Galaxy}}</ref> contained the planet [[Peridea]], the homeworld of the [[Witch Kingdom of the Dathmiri]]. These beings were led by the [[Great Mothers]], who built a [[Great Mothers' Fortress|towering fortress]] with an underground [[temple]] and a tall spire topped by a circular [[henge]]. They also used [[purrgil]] to travel the [[Intergalactic void]] between galaxies.<ref name="P6" /> They also established a [[Seatos reflex point|henge]] on the planet [[Seatos]] in [[the galaxy]] of the [[Nightsisters]] to point the [[Pathway to Peridea]].<ref name="P2">{{Ahsoka|Part Two: Toil and Trouble}}</ref> A [[star map]] which led to Peridea was also hidden at a [[Nightsisters' Temple|former Nightsister stronghold]] on [[Arcana]].<ref name="P1">{{Ahsoka|Part One: Master and Apprentice}}</ref> The Great Mothers eventually entered a type of hibernation sleep, and during this time a [[Far galaxy war|war]] broke out, which led to the far galaxy being largely dead. Planets such as Peridea became a barren wasteland and the Great Mothers way of life was wiped out.<ref name="Darkness Rising">{{HomeVideoCite|set=Ahsoka: The Complete First Season|featurette=Darkness Rising}}</ref> Although the far galaxy was depicted in some [[Star map|star charts]],<ref name="Celebration Live">{{SWYouTube|NBqHmtV9LzM|Rosario Dawson, Jon Favreau, and Dave Filoni &#124; Star Wars Celebration LIVE! 2025}}</ref> like one in the [[Jedi Archives]],<ref name="AOTC">{{Film|II}}</ref> the route to this galaxy was relegated to myth.<ref name="P2" />

===Rediscovery===
{{Quote|That is Peridea. The ancient home world of my ancestors, the Dathomiri.''"<br />"''The Jedi archives spoke of this place. It was the end of a migration route used by the star whales as they traversed the void from one galaxy to the other.''"<br />"''My people were among the first to harness and ride the creatures in the days before time was counted.''"<br />"''The whales came here to die. Peridea is a graveyard.|Morgan Elsbeth and Baylan Skoll, upon reaching the far galaxy|<ref name="P6" />}}
During the [[Liberation of Lothal]], a pod of purrgil carried [[Grand Admiral]] [[Mitth'raw'nuruodo|Thrawn]] and the [[Jedi]] rebel [[Ezra Bridger]] to Peridea.<ref name="P2" /> On Peridea, Thrawn rebuilt his [[Imperial-class Star Destroyer|Imperial Star Destroyer]] ''[[Chimaera]]'' but the damaged starship was unable to return to their home galaxy. Thrawn also awoke the Great Mothers, establishing an alliance between [[Thrawn's forces|his forces]] and the ancient [[Dathomirian]]s.<ref name="P8">{{Ahsoka|Part Eight: The Jedi, the Witch, and the Warlord}}</ref> Bridger escaped the Imperials and became the leader of a nomadic [[Noti]] clan.<ref name="P7">{{Ahsoka|Part Seven: Dreams and Madness}}</ref>

Seven years later, during the era of the [[New Republic]], [[Galactic Empire|Imperial]] loyalist and Nightsister [[Morgan Elsbeth]] ordered the construction of a massive [[hyperspace transport ring]] known as the ''[[Eye of Sion]]'' in order to bring Thrawn back to the known galaxy.<ref name="P2" /> Around that time, the former Jedi [[Ahsoka Tano]] discovered the Arcana star map. Her former apprentice [[Sabine Wren]] managed to unlock the map but it was stolen by [[Shin Hati]], a mercenary working for Elsbeth.<ref name="P1" /> Following a [[Incident on Seatos|duel]] with Tano and Wren on Seatos, [[Baylan Skoll]], Hati's master and another one of Elsbeth's mercenaries, managed to unlock the star map and relay the hyperspace coordinates to Peridea to Elsbeth. Elsbeth's forces then departed on the ''Eye of Sion'' with the captive Wren for Peridea.<ref name="P4">{{Ahsoka|Part Four: Fallen Jedi}}</ref> Using the pathway, Elsbeth's forces reached Peridea where they established contact with the Great Mothers and Thrawn's forces.<ref name="P6" /> There, they spent three cycles loading caskets from the catacombs beneath the [[Great Mothers' Fortress]].<ref name="P8" />

Tano and the Jedi [[training droid]] [[Huyang]] also traveled to the Far Galaxy with the help of a [[purrgil]] pod and reunited with Wren and Bridger.<ref name="P7" /> Following a skirmish with Tano, Wren and Bridger, Thrawn, the Great Mothers and his [[Star Destroyer]] ''[[Chimaera]]'' managed to [[Battle of Peridea|escape]] Peridea and traveled to [[Dathomir]] in the home galaxy via the ''Eye of Sion''. While Tano, Wren and Huyang were stranded on Peridea, Bridger managed to stow aboard the ''Chimaera'' and reunite with [[General]] [[Hera Syndulla]]. Hati joined the [[Bandits of Peridea]] while Skoll sought a mysterious power on the planet that was seemingly connected to the mystical beings known as [[The Ones]].<ref name="P8" />

==Behind the scenes==
The far galaxy first appeared in the [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: Ahsoka]]'', released in [[2023]].<ref name="P6" /> However, the [[Extragalactic|extra-galactic]] location itself had existed in some form since [[2018]] at least; according to [[Timothy Zahn]] in an interview at Dragon Con 2018, the location where Grand Admiral Thrawn had been sent to by the [[purrgil]] after "[[Family Reunion – and Farewell]]," the series finale of ''[[Star Wars Rebels]]'', had already been decided by that time.<ref name="2018 Zahn Interview">{{YouTube|channel=@StarWarsExplained|name=Star Wars Explained|video=GYUk_LmQKz4|text=Timothy Zahn Full Interview &ndash; Dragon Con 2018|date=2018-09-08}}</ref> The name "far galaxy" was used within ''Ahsoka'' "[[Part Two: Toil and Trouble]]"<ref name="P2" /> and the galaxy's official [[Databank (2014-)|Databank]] page, both in lower case letters.<ref name="Databank" /> A capitalized form of the name was featured in ''[[Star Wars Insider]]''.<ref name="224 Launchpad">{{InsiderCite|224|Launchpad}}</ref>

At [[Celebration Japan (2025)|Celebration Japan]], [[Dave Filoni]] revealed the idea for the far galaxy had come from the other galaxies previously pictured in star charts in the films.<ref name="Celebration Live" />

